  <iati-identifier>47045-BDI-C-CRB-1</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB/VIH/RSS Communautaire - Burundi (01-Mar-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burundi has a generalized HIV epidemic with concentrated sub-epidemics among high-risk populations.  According to the Demographic and Health Survey conducted in 2010, the average prevalence of HIV in the adult population was 1.4%.  According to the modes of transmission study (UNAIDS 2013), new HIV infections are particularly high among heterosexual couples, followed by sex workers (SW) and their clients, and men who have sex with men (MSM).  Among TB patients, HIV prevalence is 15% (WHO 2013). This program is being implemented to ensure that the objectives of the National Strategic Plan for the fight against AIDS (2014-2017), such as achieving universal access to the prevention, treatment, care and support of persons infected and affected by HIV, are met by 2017.  This will be achieved through strengthening the health and community systems, to ensure service delivery to vulnerable and affected populations.  This Principal Recipient (PR) (Croix-Rouge Burundi) is a new PR that will focus on education and support at the community level, and trainings among vulnerable populations, including miners, prisoners, Batwa community and refugee leaders, to promote access to HIV and TB services, and increase awareness of gender-based violence.  Burundi has received financial support from the Global Fund since 2003 that was implemented by previous PRs, through the Round 1, Round 5 and Round 8 grants.</narrative>
  </description>
